{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1578389333,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MTUwNzAzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3967#issuecomment-571507033"},"message":"\u003e  Then the process does something after the last update(ok) which takes a couple of hours before stating action summary and returning the prompt.\n\nThis suggests to me, that it's the final call to `save` that takes that long. `update` calls save with explicit paths to save though, so it shouldn't actually need to do an extensive status investigation. My guess is, that `update` should call `save` with `--updated`. What do you think, @mih?\n\nOther than that, we might need to be able to better control `save`'s status call, if we know what to save.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"a29d5859530e551c9c63051e6b73ecbf9e195803"},"timestamp":1578410621,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MTYzMzI4Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3967#issuecomment-571633286"},"message":"Thanks for looking into this. Would appreciate a solution as we are doing\nupdates relatively frequently.\n\nOn Tue, Jan 7, 2020 at 4:28 AM Benjamin Poldrack \u003cnotifications@github.com\u003e\nwrote:\n\n\u003e Then the process does something after the last update(ok) which takes a\n\u003e couple of hours before stating action summary and returning the prompt.\n\u003e\n\u003e This suggests to me, that it's the final call to save that takes that\n\u003e long. update calls save with explicit paths to save though, so it\n\u003e shouldn't actually need to do an extensive status investigation. My guess\n\u003e is, that update should call save with --updated. What do you think, @mih\n\u003e \u003chttps://github.com/mih\u003e?\n\u003e\n\u003e Other than that, we might need to be able to better control save's status\n\u003e call, if we know what to save.\n\u003e\n\u003e —\n\u003e You are receiving this because you authored the thread.\n\u003e Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n\u003e \u003chttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3967?email_source=notifications\u0026email_token=ACFJU7MMIDCAWHT7FFD3P4DQ4RDNNA5CNFSM4KAHMN62YY3PNVWWK3TUL52HS4DFVREXG43VMVBW63LNMVXHJKTDN5WW2ZLOORPWSZGOEIIICWI#issuecomment-571507033\u003e,\n\u003e or unsubscribe\n\u003e \u003chttps://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/ACFJU7IK46ZJXLXQ75GGPD3Q4RDNNANCNFSM4KAHMN6Q\u003e\n\u003e .\n\u003e","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1578411918,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MTY0Mjg2Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3967#issuecomment-571642862"},"message":"Meanwhile you could try using stable release 0.11.8 (eg installed in a virtualenv) - how slow update would work there?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"a29d5859530e551c9c63051e6b73ecbf9e195803"},"timestamp":1578412545,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MTY0NzU4Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3967#issuecomment-571647586"},"message":"@yarikoptic Can you give me the pip install command for 0.11.8 (I guess via github)?\n\nI was under the impression that 0.12 was the most cutting edge version, and that is what we have used so far. So I hope there is no problem when \"downgrading\" to 0.11.8.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1578414963,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MTY2NjcxMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3967#issuecomment-571666711"},"message":"\u003e @yarikoptic Can you give me the pip install command for 0.11.8 (I guess via github)?\n\n`pip install datalad` or more specific `pip install datalad==0.11.8` should do it\n\n\u003e I was under the impression that 0.12 was the most cutting edge version, and that is what we have used so far. So I hope there is no problem when \"downgrading\" to 0.11.8.\n\nyes - 0.12.x is \"cutting edge\" (but not yet released, only release-candidates). 0.11.x series is considered to be the \"stable\" one (no cutting edge developments), although 0.12 might have addressed some bugs which still linger in 0.11.x.\n\nYou don't need to \"downgrade\".  Just create a new virtualenv and install whatever other version of datalad you want to use there.  E.g.\n\n```\nvirtualenv --system-site-packages venv-datalad-0.11\nsource venv-datalad-0.11/bin/activate\npip install datalad==0.11.8\n```\nand when you want to get back to \"default one\", just issue `deactivate` command.\nLet me know how it goes","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"a29d5859530e551c9c63051e6b73ecbf9e195803"},"timestamp":1578448836,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MTg1NzM0OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3967#issuecomment-571857349"},"message":"Thanks @yarikoptic . I don't have an update for the big 1.3Tb dataset right now, but I will switch to 0.11.8 and see how things are going. Will report back. You can close this issue or keep it open.\n\nNote also that I am using metalad and neuroimaging extensions. Just letting you know because I see tons of new features in 0.12 starting from almost 1 year ago.\nhttp://docs.datalad.org/en/latest/changelog.html","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"a29d5859530e551c9c63051e6b73ecbf9e195803"},"timestamp":1578448836,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDMzNDA2MDc0Mg=="},"target":"cf509afed1216357008cbbf62f919908c592fbbe4f478d535388c4322cda86ab","message":"Thanks @yarikoptic . I don't have an update for the big 1.3Tb dataset right now, but I will switch to 0.11.8 and see how things are going. Will report back. You can close this issue or keep it open.\n\nNote also that I am using metalad and neuroimaging extensions. Just letting you know because I see tons of new features in 0.12 starting from almost 1 year ago, including extensions stuff.\nhttp://docs.datalad.org/en/latest/changelog.html","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1578451235,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MTg2NjE3OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3967#issuecomment-571866178"},"message":"\u003e Thanks @yarikoptic . I don't have an update for the big 1.3Tb dataset right now, but I will switch to 0.11.8 and see how things are going.\n\nyou could run and compare `time datalad update -r --merge` on both 0.12 and 0.11.x even now - could be informative.\n\n\u003e You can close this issue or keep it open.\n\nwill be happy to get it closed whenever it is \"addressed\".  AFAIK it is not yet.\n\n\u003e new features in 0.12 starting from almost 1 year ago, including extensions stuff.\n\nFWIW many extensions (but not metalad) as still compatible with 0.11.x.","files":null}]}